        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9a4a5faf-17e7-57b1-bb24-e205b6f3ccd2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Dubai, Bur Dubai, Deira, Dubai Creek, Jumeirah Village, United Arab Emirates\n- Markets: Dubai Textile Souk, Dubai Spice Souk, Dubai Gold Souk\n- Religious Sites: Iranian Mosque\n- Buildings: Nili Tower\n\nFacts:\n- The Dubai Textile Souk, also known as the Old Textile Souk, is a traditional textile market in the historic Bur Dubai neighbourhood of Dubai.\n- Across Dubai Creek from the Dubai Textile Souk in Deira are the Dubai Spice Souk and Dubai Gold Souk, which are accessible by special abra boats.\n- The Dubai Gold Souk consists of over 300 retailers, most of whom are jewellery traders.\n- The Iranian Mosque, also known as the Ali ibn Abi Talib Iranian Mosque, is a Shia mosque near the old Dubai Textile Souk in Bur Dubai, Dubai, United Arab Emirates.\n- The Nili Tower is a 57-floor tower in Jumeirah Village, Dubai, United Arab Emirates.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
